-- title:
--   Inertia-fixed place on an annulus over a fixed value
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$, and let $F =$ `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) F₀` be the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise image of $F_0$. Let `An` be an annulus for $A$ in $F$: a set `An.dom` of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, proper, with principal ideals), a parameter `An.param` $\in F$ and a modulus `An.modulus` in the maximal ideal of $A$, such that every $P \in$ `An.dom` is rational (its residue field is generated by $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), has `An.param` in its valuation ring with nonzero value $P(\mathrm{param}) \in \mathfrak{m}_A$ dividing the modulus inside $\mathfrak{m}_A$, such that each admissible value is attained by exactly one place of the domain, that $\mathrm{ord}_P(\mathrm{param} - P(\mathrm{param})) = 1$, and the unit principle. Write $I_A \subseteq \mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ for the image of the inertia subgroup of $A$ inside its decomposition group, acting on $F$ and on places through the coefficientwise semilinear automorphisms `arithmeticGalois F₀`. Assume `An.param` is fixed by every $\sigma \in I_A$ and `An.dom` is stable under $I_A$. Then for every $c \in A$ lying in the maximal ideal of $A$, nonzero in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with `An.modulus` $= c\,m$ for some $m \in \mathfrak{m}_A$, and with $\sigma(c) = c$ for all $\sigma \in I_A$, there is a place $W \in$ `An.dom` fixed by every $\sigma \in I_A$ and with $W$-value of `An.param` equal to $c$.
--
--   This is the statement that an annulus whose parameter and domain are inertia-invariant has, at each inertia-invariant admissible value of the parameter, an inertia-invariant point of its domain; the values $c$ correspond to the integral depths inside an annulus attached to a node of a semistable model. It is used in the analysis of specialisation of places on modular curves, in [`ModularCurve.JHPlaceSpecialization.comp_surjective_of_depthCompLaw_of_annulusInf`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHPlaceSpecialization.comp_surjective_of_depthCompLaw_of_annulusInf) and in [`ModularCurve.JHPlaceSpecialization.exists_annulusPositionLaw_inertiaInvariant_exists_fixed_of_annulus`](thm.html#ModularCurve.JHPlaceSpecialization.exists_annulusPositionLaw_inertiaInvariant_exists_fixed_of_annulus).
